  "configuration_id": "config_011",
  "reason": "Existing evidence shows RNA strongly benefits from multiprofile avgpool (config_002: 0.591 accuracy / 0.573 F1), while transformer and singleprofile are weaker. Image ResNet is only tested as singleprofile and is weak (config_010: 0.208 accuracy / 0.172 F1), so it is unclear whether the image modality is intrinsically weak or simply underrepresented by the singleprofile/no-aggregation setting. config_011 tests the same ResNet image encoder under multiprofile avgpool, the profile/aggregation pipeline that helped RNA, while avoiding simultaneous changes to modality or fusion. This is the best next experiment because it reduces uncertainty about the image main effect before investing limited budget in multimodal fusion; if image improves, multimodal configs become more promising, and if it remains weak, the search can focus on RNA improvements."
}

